What are we building, fixing, or destroying today?
==================================================

The line under the greeting read "Explore a question, work with your files, or make something
useful." — a product sentence written by somebody imagining a user who needs to be told what a
workspace is for. What it should say, on a desktop you already know the purpose of, is the question
that is actually being asked of the machine.

"Sup bitch?" stays. The subtitle is now "What are we building, fixing, or destroying today?"
